# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mercy Blade — Environment Variables (IAP subset)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file documents the environment variables the Apple In-App Purchase
# track introduced. Other Vite env vars (Supabase URL, anon key, Stripe
# price IDs, analytics keys, etc.) belong to other tracks and are not
# catalogued here. Treat this as additive — copy the relevant rows into
# your own .env.local / deployment env.
#
# Convention:
#   VITE_*      → exposed to the browser bundle (must be non-secret).
#   REVENUECAT_*→ server-only; set via `supabase secrets set` (never
#                 prefixed VITE_).
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Apple In-App Purchase (iOS only)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# RevenueCat iOS SDK public key. Safe to ship in the iOS bundle; RevenueCat
# designed this key to live in client code. Not needed on web or Android.
#
# Where to find: RevenueCat Dashboard → Project → API Keys → Apple App Store.
# Two flavors exist ("appl_…" = production, "test_…" = sandbox/TestFlight);
# you can use either value — RevenueCat routes based on the receipt type.
#
# If missing at runtime on iOS: initRevenueCat() logs a warning and
# IapPlanCard renders a "not configured" state. App does NOT crash.
VITE_REVENUECAT_APPLE_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RevenueCat → Supabase webhook (server-side only; DO NOT prefix VITE_)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared secret for the revenuecat-webhook edge function. Set the same value
# in RevenueCat Dashboard → Integrations → Webhook → Authorization header,
# AND in Supabase Edge Function secrets with the command below.
#
# Generate a fresh token locally:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Apply as a Supabase secret:
#   npx supabase secrets set REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH_TOKEN=<value> \
#     --project-ref buemdfxyhxunzpgdoqin
#
# Then paste the same <value> into RevenueCat's Authorization field.
# The webhook handler accepts either the bare token or "Bearer <token>",
# so either format works in the dashboard.
REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional kill switch for the webhook. Set this to the literal string
# "true" to make revenuecat-webhook return 200 without writing anything
# to the DB. Useful if the webhook is emitting bad data and you need
# to freeze writes WITHOUT redeploying the function.
#
# Apply:
#   npx supabase secrets set REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_DISABLED=true \
#     --project-ref buemdfxyhxunzpgdoqin
#
# Unset (re-enable):
#   npx supabase secrets unset REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_DISABLED \
#     --project-ref buemdfxyhxunzpgdoqin
REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_DISABLED=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry — error & crash reporting (web + iOS + Android via @sentry/capacitor)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# DSN for the Sentry project that ingests web JS errors, native iOS crashes,
# and native Android crashes. The DSN is a client-side credential designed
# to be public in the bundle, but we still source it from env so it can be
# rotated without a code change.
#
# Activation model:
#   - Empty value → Sentry is fully no-op. The @sentry/capacitor + @sentry/react
#     SDKs are dynamically imported only when this is set, so an unset DSN
#     keeps the bundle clean (zero KB of Sentry shipped).
#   - Set in Vercel project env vars (production scope only). Do not commit
#     the real value here.
#
# Where to find: Sentry Dashboard → Settings → Client Keys (DSN).
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry source-map upload (BUILD-TIME, server-only — DO NOT prefix VITE_)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These three are read by @sentry/vite-plugin in vite.config.ts during
# `vite build`. They are NOT runtime vars and must NOT carry the VITE_
# prefix — that would leak the auth token into the browser bundle.
#
# Activation model (see vite.config.ts L100–119 / L457–460):
#   - All three set → the plugin uploads source maps to Sentry and sets
#     build.sourcemap = "hidden": .map files are generated, uploaded,
#     then deleted (filesToDeleteAfterUpload), and the shipped JS has no
#     //# sourceMappingURL comment. Clients never see source maps;
#     Sentry can still de-mangle production stack traces.
#   - Any one missing → the plugin is a no-op and no source maps are
#     emitted. This is the correct, safe path for laptop / CI builds
#     with no token. Do NOT "fix" a local build that skips upload.
#
# Where these belong: the Vercel project's Production environment
# variables (Settings → Environment Variables). They are NOT set in
# this repo's GitHub Actions deploy workflows — production deploys are
# Vercel-native, so the Vercel build is the only place that needs them.
# After adding them, trigger a redeploy; source maps apply to errors
# from that release forward (pre-existing minified issues stay minified).

# Sentry org slug. Canonical value for this project: mercy-blade
# (not a secret — already present in .github/workflows/sentry-auto-fix.yml).
SENTRY_ORG=

# Sentry project slug. Canonical value for this project: mercyblade-web
# (not a secret — already present in .github/workflows/sentry-auto-fix.yml).
SENTRY_PROJECT=

# Sentry auth token — the one real SECRET here. Generate at
#   https://sentry.io/settings/account/api/auth-tokens/
# with scopes: project:read, project:releases, org:read.
#
# Set ONLY in Vercel's Production env vars. NEVER commit the real value
# to this repo. (A separate SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN exists as a GitHub Actions
# secret for the sentry-auto-fix workflow — that secret store is NOT
# visible to the Vercel build, so the Vercel value must be set too.)
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Cloud TTS — Vietnamese audio (local script only, not used at runtime)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Path to the Google Cloud service-account JSON key with Cloud TTS API access.
# Used by scripts/generate-vietnamese-audio.ts to generate A2-C2 audio clips
# and upload them to Supabase Storage via the vi-VN-Wavenet-A / -B voices.
#
# Server-side / local-only secret. NEVER prefix with VITE_ — this must not
# ship in the browser bundle.
#
# Where to find: https://console.cloud.google.com → IAM & Admin →
# Service Accounts → keys. Save the JSON locally and point at its path.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=  # Path to Google Cloud service account JSON key

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Microsoft Clarity — session replay + heatmaps (free, unlimited)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Clarity project ID. When set, the Clarity tag loads on app boot —
# but ONLY after the same marketing-consent gate that Pixel/GA4 use
# (default ON, opt-out wins; see src/services/behaviorTrackingFlag.ts)
# and only via the deferred init so it never blocks first paint.
# Empty / unset → Clarity never loads (no-op, no console noise).
#
# VITE_ prefix: required so it reaches the browser bundle. NOT a secret
# (a Clarity project ID is public by design — it ships in the tag URL).
#
# Where to find: https://clarity.microsoft.com → create a project named
# "MercyBlade" → Settings → the project ID (short alphanumeric string).
#
# Set in Vercel PRODUCTION env vars only. Recommend NOT setting it in
# Preview env (keep staging/preview sessions unrecorded).
#
# Privacy: sensitive surfaces carry data-clarity-mask="true" in code
# (Mercy chat input, placement test, auth email/password). Also set the
# Clarity dashboard masking mode to "Strict" for defence in depth.
VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=  # Microsoft Clarity project ID (prod only)
